Ways to have IPv4 and IPv6 compatable with eachother

Dual Stack
    - Allows coexistence operation of both IPv4 and IPv6 protocols on the same network infratructure
    - Prefers IPv6, but will fallback on IPv4

Tunneling
    - Encapsulates packets of a different protocol
    - IPv6 packets encapsulated within IPv4 packets

NAT64
    - Network address translation mechanism
    - Allows IPv6-only devices to communicate with IPv4 servers and services
    - Involves a NAT gateway that translates IPv6 into IPv4 before travel and vice versa